56":"sha256:7ffdc1b3c2a5f2dea88d3e70490c6b9004dd3a4ea09ef14f3e3720ce2150f89e","file":"preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":10,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"d2595dd5c3f7699d5e5aa1b70a4751af98ad0999fabbd03b51cb2e9475a4aef4","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:7ffdc1b3c2a5f2dea88d3e70490c6b9004dd3a4ea09ef14f3e3720ce2150f89e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Euclidean-Steinitz-Bergstrom-theorem-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L10"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:signing}\nThere is an absolute constant $C$ such that, for all integers $d,N\\ge1$ and\nevery sequence $v_1,\\ldots,v_N\\in\\R^d$ with $\\lVert v_i\\rVert_2\\le1$,\nthere are signs $\\varepsilon_1,\\ldots,\\varepsilon_N\\in\\{-1,1\\}$ for which\n\\[\n \\max_{0\\le k\\le N}\n \\left\\lVert\\sum_{i=1}^k\\varepsilon_i v_i\\right\\rVert_2\\le C\\sqrt d.\n\\]\nThe same signs control all prefixes, and $C$ is independent of $d$, $N$\nand the sequence."}
